  </a>

  <!-- INTRO -->
  <section class="intro">
    <h2>OUR SERVICE AGREEMENT</h2>
    <p>
      Welcome to Pour Live. These Terms of Service describe
      the conditions governing the use of our website,
      booking requests, and private event bartending services.
    </p>
    <p>
      By submitting a booking request, accepting a written quote,
      or engaging Pour Live for an event, you acknowledge these
      terms. A confirmed booking may also be governed by a
      separate written event agreement.
    </p>
    <p>
      If a signed event agreement contains terms that differ
      from this page, the signed agreement will control for
      that event, subject to applicable law.
    </p>
    <div class="updated">
      Last Updated: November 10, 2026
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- SUMMARY -->
  <div class="summary">
    <div class="summary-card">
      <h3>CLIENT-SUPPLIED ALCOHOL</h3>
      <p>
        Pour Live provides bartending services.
        We do not sell or supply alcoholic beverages.
        Clients or authorized venues provide alcohol
        in accordance with applicable law.
      </p>
    </div>

    <div class="summary-card">
      <h3>CONFIRMED BOOKINGS</h3>
      <p>
        Submitting an event inquiry does not automatically
        reserve your date. Bookings are confirmed through
        written acceptance and any applicable payment requirements.
      </p>
    </div>

    <div class="summary-card">
      <h3>RESPONSIBLE SERVICE</h3>
      <p>
        Our bartenders may refuse alcohol service when required
        by law or when a guest's condition or behavior
        creates a safety concern.
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>

  <!-- TERMS -->
  <main class="terms">
    <h2 class="terms-heading">BOOKING POLICIES &amp; CONDITIONS</h2>

    <section class="term">
      <h2>01. ACCEPTANCE OF TERMS</h2>
      <p>
        These Terms of Service apply to visitors using the
        Pour Live website and clients requesting or purchasing
        private event bartending services.
      </p>
      <p>
        Clients booking an event must be at least 18 years old
        and legally capable of entering into a binding agreement.
      </p>
      <p>
        The individual submitting the booking request represents
        that they are authorized to make arrangements for the event.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="term">
      <h2>02. SERVICES PROVIDED</h2>
      <p>
        Pour Live provides professional bartending services for
        private events, including weddings, birthdays, corporate
        gatherings, banquets, celebrations, and other approved occasions.
      </p>
      <p>Depending on the selected package, services may include:</p>
      <ul>
        <li>Beer and wine service</li>
        <li>Mixed drinks and classic cocktails</li>
        <li>Signature cocktail preparation</li>
        <li>Bar station setup and cleanup</li>
        <li>Drink menu assistance</li>
        <li>Approved event-specific add-ons</li>
      </ul>
      <p>
        Services are limited to those specifically included
        in the accepted event quote or written agreement.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="term">
      <h2>03. ALCOHOL RESPONSIBILITIES</h2>
      <div class="highlight">
        <p>
          <strong>Important:</strong> Pour Live is a private
          bartending service. We do not sell, furnish, or supply
          alcoholic beverages as part of our standard services.
        </p>
      </div>
      <p>
        The client or authorized venue is responsible for purchasing
        and providing all alcoholic beverages intended for event service.
      </p>
      <p>
        Alcohol must be legally obtained, and its possession,
        distribution, and consumption must comply with applicable
        state and local laws.
      </p>
      <p>
        The client is responsible for ensuring the event location
        permits the planned alcohol service and for obtaining any
        permits, approvals, or licenses required of the client or venue.
      </p>
      <p>
        Pour Live reserves the right to decline any service arrangement
        that would violate applicable alcohol regulations.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="term">
      <h2>04. BOOKING REQUESTS &amp; CONFIRMATION</h2>
      <p>
        Event inquiries submitted through our website are requests
        for service, not guaranteed reservations.
      </p>
      <p>
        A booking is considered confirmed only after Pour Live
        provides written confirmation and any required payment
        conditions have been satisfied.
      </p>
      <p>
        Pour Live may decline requests based on staffing availability,
        travel distance, event requirements, venue restrictions,
        or other operational considerations.
      </p>
      <p>
        Clients must provide accurate information regarding event
        location, date, attendance, service hours, and requested services.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="term">
      <h2>05. PRICING &amp; MINIMUM SERVICE HOURS</h2>
      <p>
        Unless otherwise stated in a written quote, Pour Live's
        standard pricing is calculated per bartender, per hour.
      </p>
      <p>
        A <strong>four-hour minimum</strong> applies to
        standard event bookings.
      </p>
      <p>Current advertised starting rates include:</p>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Beer &amp; Wine:</strong> $50 per bartender, per hour</li>
        <li><strong>Full Bar:</strong> $60 per bartender, per hour</li>
        <li><strong>Signature Cocktails:</strong> $70 per bartender, per hour</li>
      </ul>
      <p>
        Pricing may vary depending on event requirements,
        staffing, add-ons, travel, and peak dates.
      </p>
      <p>
        Website estimates are informational and are not final
        binding quotes. The accepted written quote establishes
        the applicable event pricing.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="term">
      <h2>06. STAFFING REQUIREMENTS</h2>
      <p>
        Pour Live generally estimates one bartender for every 50 guests.
      </p>
      <p>
        Events exceeding that ratio may require additional bartenders
        to maintain reasonable service standards and guest safety.
      </p>
      <p>
        Final staffing requirements may also depend on the complexity
        of the drink menu, event layout, service style, and expected guest volume.
      </p>
      <p>
        Additional staffing costs will be disclosed in the event quote.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="term">
      <h2>07. TRAVEL &amp; HOLIDAY FEES</h2>
      <p>
        Standard travel pricing is based on distance from Riverside, California.
      </p>
      <ul>
        <li>Within 25 miles: no additional travel charge</li>
        <li>26–40 miles: $25 travel charge</li>
        <li>41–60 miles: $50 travel charge</li>
        <li>Beyond 60 miles: individually quoted</li>
      </ul>
      <p>
        Events occurring during designated holidays or peak-demand dates
        may be subject to a <strong>25% surcharge</strong>.
      </p>
      <p>
        Applicable fees will be identified in the final event quote.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="term">
      <h2>08. DEPOSITS &amp; PAYMENTS</h2>
      <p>
        Pour Live may require a deposit or advance payment
        to secure an event reservation.
      </p>
      <p>
        Any deposit amount, payment deadline, remaining balance,
        and accepted payment method will be provided in writing
        before booking confirmation.
      </p>
      <p>
        Clients are responsible for paying all agreed charges
        according to the payment schedule in their booking agreement.
      </p>
      <p>
        Additional services or approved extensions may result
        in additional charges.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="term">
      <h2>09. CANCELLATIONS &amp; RESCHEDULING</h2>
      <p>
        Clients requesting cancellation or rescheduling should
        notify Pour Live as soon as possible through the contact
        information provided below.
      </p>
      <p>
        Any applicable cancellation fees, deposit refunds,
        or rescheduling conditions will be determined by
        the written booking agreement and applicable law.
      </p>
      <p>
        Rescheduling is subject to staff availability
        and may require a revised quote.
      </p>
      <p>
        If Pour Live must cancel a confirmed booking,
        we will notify the client promptly and address
        any payments according to the agreement and applicable law.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="term">
      <h2>10. EVENT LOCATION &amp; SETUP</h2>
      <p>
        The client must provide a safe and accessible service
        location suitable for professional bartending.
      </p>
      <p>
        Unless separately agreed, the client or venue is
        responsible for providing the necessary bar space,
        tables, electrical access, running water, and other
        venue facilities required for the selected service.
      </p>
      <p>
        Specific supplies and equipment included in each
        package will be identified in the accepted quote.
      </p>
      <p>
        Pour Live may decline unsafe working conditions
        or request reasonable adjustments before beginning service.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="term">
      <h2>11. GUEST CONDUCT &amp; RESPONSIBLE ALCOHOL SERVICE</h2>
      <p>
        Pour Live is committed to responsible alcohol service.
      </p>
      <p>
        Bartenders may request valid identification and refuse
        alcoholic beverages to anyone under the legal drinking age.
      </p>
      <p>
        Service may also be refused to individuals who appear
        intoxicated, behave aggressively, threaten staff,
        or otherwise create a safety concern.
      </p>
      <p>
        The client is responsible for maintaining a safe event
        environment and coordinating guest management or
        security when appropriate.
      </p>
      <p>
        Pour Live may suspend or discontinue service when
        continuing would be unlawful or present a substantial safety risk.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="term">
      <h2>12. SERVICE HOURS &amp; OVERTIME</h2>
      <p>
        Bartending services are provided during the hours
        specified in the confirmed booking.
      </p>
      <p>
        Requests to extend service beyond the scheduled end time
        are subject to bartender availability, venue restrictions,
        and applicable laws.
      </p>
      <p>
        Additional time must be approved by Pour Live
        and may be billed at the applicable hourly rate.
      </p>
      <p>
        Clients should not assume that bartenders will remain
        beyond the contracted service period without prior authorization.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="term">
      <h2>13. EQUIPMENT &amp; PROPERTY</h2>
      <p>
        Pour Live may bring bartending tools and approved
        service equipment required for the event.
      </p>
      <p>
        Equipment provided by Pour Live remains its property
        unless otherwise agreed in writing.
      </p>
      <p>
        Clients are responsible for promptly reporting equipment
        damage or property incidents occurring during the event.
      </p>
      <p>
        Responsibility for damage or loss will be determined
        under the booking agreement and applicable law.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="term">
      <h2>14. TIPS &amp; GRATUITIES</h2>
      <p>
        Tips are appreciated but are not automatically required
        unless an agreed gratuity or service charge is expressly
        included in the final quote.
      </p>
      <p>
        Tip jars may be used where permitted by the client and venue.
      </p>
      <p>
        Any mandatory service charges will be disclosed
        before booking confirmation.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="term">
      <h2>15. EVENT CHANGES</h2>
      <p>
        Clients must notify Pour Live of significant changes
        to their event, including:
      </p>
      <ul>
        <li>Event date or start time</li>
        <li>Event location or venue</li>
        <li>Expected guest attendance</li>
        <li>Requested drink menu</li>
        <li>Service duration</li>
        <li>Additional staffing requirements</li>
      </ul>
      <p>
        Changes may affect staffing availability, pricing,
        and the services we can provide.
